### Demo 3: a bind mount maps a host directory into the container

$ echo "edited from the host" > ~/lab2-bindmount-data/host-note.txt
$ docker run --rm -v ~/lab2-bindmount-data:/data ubuntu:24.04 cat /data/host-note.txt
edited from the host

$ docker run --rm -v ~/lab2-bindmount-data:/data ubuntu:24.04 sh -c "echo written-by-container >> /data/host-note.txt"
$ cat ~/lab2-bindmount-data/host-note.txt   (on the host)
edited from the host
written-by-container
--> both sides see the same file: bind mount is synced with the host filesystem
